#. Tag: title
#: tutorial.docbook:34
#, no-c-format
msgid "A Step-By-Step Tutorial"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:36
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In this chapter, &kpresenter; is introduced using a simple tutorial. We "
"shall walk through the most basic steps that are involved in creating a "
"presentation, and adding some basic effects."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: tutorial.docbook:43
#, no-c-format
msgid "Start a new document"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:45
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you start &kpresenter;, the usual &koffice; startup dialog appears."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: tutorial.docbook:50
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guilabel>&koffice;</guilabel> startup dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: tutorial.docbook:55
#, no-c-format
msgid "The &koffice; startup dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:59
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select <guilabel>Screen</guilabel> on the left then select the template "
"labeled <guilabel>Title</guilabel> (highlighted in blue in the screenshot "
"above) by clicking on it. You can check <guilabel>Always use this template</"
"guilabel> to make it the default template."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:66
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Now click <guibutton>Use This Template</guibutton>. This brings up the slide "
"editor window, where you can view and edit the slides (and objects contained "
"in them) in your document. At the moment, we just have one slide, with one "
"object on it, which is a text box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: tutorial.docbook:74
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>The slide editor</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: tutorial.docbook:77
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The slide editor</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:81
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Double-click the text box. The cursor changes to a vertical bar to show that "
"you can now type some text and the background of the edited area becomes "
"grey."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: tutorial.docbook:88
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>The text insertion cursor</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: tutorial.docbook:92
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The text insertion cursor</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:96
#, no-c-format
msgid "Go ahead, type some text!"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: tutorial.docbook:101
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Adding text</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: tutorial.docbook:105
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Adding text</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:109
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click away from the text to de-select the text box when you are done typing."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: tutorial.docbook:117
#, no-c-format
msgid "Add a new page"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:119
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Let's now add a new slide to our document. To do so, click the "
"<guimenu>Insert</guimenu> menu, and then click on <guimenuitem>Slide...</"
"guimenuitem>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: tutorial.docbook:126
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Inserting a slide from the menu</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: tutorial.docbook:130
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Inserting a slide from the menu</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:134
#, no-c-format
msgid "This brings up the <guilabel>Insert Slide</guilabel> dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: tutorial.docbook:139
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>The <guilabel>Insert Slide</guilabel> dialog</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: tutorial.docbook:143
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The <guilabel>Insert Slide</guilabel> dialog</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:148
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select <guilabel>Choose different template</guilabel> and click "
"<guibutton>OK</guibutton> to add a new page after page 1."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:153
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The startup dialog comes up so that we can decide what the new slide should "
"look like. This time, select <guilabel>Screen</guilabel> on the left and "
"double click on the <guilabel>One Column</guilabel> template (highlighted in "
"blue.)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: tutorial.docbook:160
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Choosing a template for the new page</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: tutorial.docbook:163
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Choosing a template for the new page</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:168
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The new slide now appears in the editing window. To change between pages of "
"your presentation, you can select slides in the pane to the left "
"(highlighted in blue for this screenshot)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: tutorial.docbook:175
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>The slides list</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: tutorial.docbook:178
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The slides list</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:182
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The newly inserted slide has two text boxes. There is one for a title, and "
"another to contain a bulleted list of items."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: tutorial.docbook:188
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>The new slide</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: tutorial.docbook:191
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The new slide</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:195
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Double-click and type a title. Then double-click on the second text box with "
"the bullet. Type some text and end the paragraph by pressing the "
"<keycap>Enter</keycap> or <keycap>Return</keycap> key. As you type new "
"paragraphs, bullets automatically appear in front of them."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: tutorial.docbook:203
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Adding text to the second slide</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: tutorial.docbook:206
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Adding text to the second slide</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:210
#, no-c-format
msgid "You can de-select the text box by clicking away from it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: tutorial.docbook:217
#, no-c-format
msgid "Insert a picture"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:219
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Let's go back to the first slide now. Use the list of slides on the left of "
"your screen."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:224
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In this section, we'll liven our presentation up a bit by adding a nice logo "
"to the title page. To do so, the first step is to click on the "
"<guimenu>Insert</guimenu> menu item, and then on <guimenuitem>Picture...</"
"guimenuitem>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: tutorial.docbook:232
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Using the menu to add an image</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: tutorial.docbook:235
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Using the menu to add an image</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:239
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This brings up a file selection dialog. To learn about this or other "
"standard &kde; dialog boxes in detail, please consult the &kde; "
"documentation. You can browse by clicking on <guiicon>folder</guiicon> icons "
"or by using the <guiicon>browser</guiicon> style buttons on the toolbar "
"(highlighted in red.) Clicking the <guiicon>up arrow</guiicon> takes you up "
"one folder level."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:248
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Find the file named <filename>koffice-logo.png</filename>, which may be in a "
"different folder than the one shown in the screenshot below. You can also "
"choose any other graphic file if you like! Select the file, and click "
"<guibutton>OK</guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: tutorial.docbook:256
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Choosing a picture to add</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: tutorial.docbook:259
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Choosing a picture to add</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:263
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click with the &LMB; where you want to place the loge in it's original size "
"or draw a rectangle with the left mouse (click the &LMB; and keep the button "
"pressed) to specify the position and size for the logo. There are selection "
"handles (little squares) visible around the border of the graphic."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: tutorial.docbook:270
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>The newly added image</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: tutorial.docbook:273
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The newly added image</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:277
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Place the mouse cursor anywhere in the middle of the logo, and drag it to "
"the middle of the title page. Then use the selection handles to resize it "
"correctly."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: tutorial.docbook:284
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Dragging and resizing the image</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: tutorial.docbook:287
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Dragging and resizing the image</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:291
#, no-c-format
msgid "That's it. Now you have a picture on the title page!"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: tutorial.docbook:298
#, no-c-format
msgid "Insert a &koffice; object"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:299
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Let's insert another &koffice; object under the picture, for example a chart."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:302
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Every &koffice; supported document can be embedded in a &kpresenter; slide. "
"Let's choose a chart from &kchart;. To do so, the first step is to click on "
"the <guimenu>Insert</guimenu> menu item, and then on <guisubmenu>Object</"
"guisubmenu>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: tutorial.docbook:310
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>The Insert Object menu</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: tutorial.docbook:313
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The Insert Object menu</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:317
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A list of the &koffice; available components appears as submenu. Select "
"<guilabel>Chart</guilabel> and then outline with your mouse the area you "
"want to put your chart in on the &kpresenter; slide."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: tutorial.docbook:324
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Select the area where to put the chart</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: tutorial.docbook:327
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Select the area where to put the chart</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:334
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once you release the mouse button, a blank chart is added on the slide. "
"Whenever you work in the chart, the toolbars and menubar in &kpresenter; "
"main window are replaced by those from &kchart;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: tutorial.docbook:341
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>&kchart; menus and toolbars embedded</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: tutorial.docbook:344
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>&kchart; menus and toolbars embedded</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:348
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"While you are in the chart, clicking with the &RMB; will bring the &kchart; "
"settings menu which allows you to modify the parameters of the chart. Please "
"see the &kchart; user manual to get more information on how to use &kchart;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:353
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click anywhere with the &LMB; outside the chart to go back to &kpresenter; "
"slide."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:356
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A single click on the chart will allow you to drag it to change its location "
"and also to drag the borders to make it bigger as with any other "
"&kpresenter; object. Double click on the chart to get into &kchart; mode and "
"modify any of the chart property."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: tutorial.docbook:364
#, no-c-format
msgid "Add a shadow to the title text"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:366
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Let's continue enhancing our title page by adding a shadow behind the title. "
"<mousebutton>Right</mousebutton> click anywhere on the title text. This "
"achieves two things: the text box containing the title is selected, and a "
"menu pops up."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:373
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select the <guimenuitem>Shadow Objects...</guimenuitem> option in the popup "
"menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: tutorial.docbook:378
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>The context menu</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: tutorial.docbook:381
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The context menu</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:385
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Shadow</guilabel> dialog pops up. The distance between the "
"shadow and the text is currently 0 so the shadow cannot be seen (this part "
"of the dialog box is highlighted in red.)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: tutorial.docbook:392
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>The <guilabel>Shadow</guilabel> dialog</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: tutorial.docbook:395
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The <guilabel>Shadow</guilabel> dialog</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:400
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Increase the distance value to 3. The effect of changing the distance can be "
"seen in the preview window. Now click <guibutton>OK</guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: tutorial.docbook:406
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Adding a shadow to the title</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: tutorial.docbook:409
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Adding a shadow to the title</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:413
#, no-c-format
msgid "Now the title has a shadow!"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: tutorial.docbook:418
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>The new shadowed title</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: tutorial.docbook:421
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The new shadowed title</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: tutorial.docbook:428
#, no-c-format
msgid "Change the color of the title text"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:430
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Let's finish by changing the color of the title text from black to blue. To "
"do so, select the title text by double-clicking the text box and select the "
"text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:435
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Open the <guilabel>Select Color</guilabel> dialog by clicking on the "
"<guiicon>dark blue A</guiicon> icon on the right side of the <guilabel>Text</"
"guilabel> toolbar (this icon has a Color... tooltip) or choose the "
"<guimenu>Text</guimenu> menu and then click on <guimenuitem>Color...</"
"guimenuitem> and change the color to blue."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: tutorial.docbook:442
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>The color palette</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: tutorial.docbook:445
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The color palette</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:449
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click <guibutton>OK</guibutton> in the <guilabel>Select Color</guilabel> "
"dialog. Changing the color of the selected text to blue changes its "
"appearance. The exact color that highlighted text turns depends on your "
"system color scheme."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: tutorial.docbook:456
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Highlighted text</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: tutorial.docbook:459
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Highlighted text</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:463
#, no-c-format
msgid "Now click away from the text to de-select it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: tutorial.docbook:468
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>The finished title</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: tutorial.docbook:471
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The finished title</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:475
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Now that there are two slides, why not try a slide show! To start the slide "
"show, press the <guiicon>play</guiicon> button (the blue double arrow) on "
"the <guilabel>Slide Show</guilabel> toolbar. The first slide should appear "
"on your screen."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: tutorial.docbook:482
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>The first slide</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: tutorial.docbook:485
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The first slide</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:489
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To advance from the first slide to the next, just click anywhere on the "
"screen, or use the <keycap>Page Down</keycap> key."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: tutorial.docbook:495
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>The second slide</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: tutorial.docbook:498
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The second slide</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:502
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To exit the slide show, <mousebutton>right</mousebutton> click, and then "
"select the <guimenuitem>End</guimenuitem> option from the popup menu."
msgstr ""
